hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15745","Affan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Khatmi, he said: Umarah ibn Khuzaymah and al-Harith ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Qurad, he said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing Hajj, and I saw him come out of the privy, so I followed him with a water skin or a cup, and sat for him on the road, and when he relieved himself he would go far."
"15746","Affan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far Umayr ibn Yazid narrated to me, he said: al-Harith ibn Fudayl and Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Qurad, he said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing Hajj. He said: He camped at a station and came out of the privy, so I followed him with a water skin or a cup, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended to relieve himself, would go far. I sat for him on the road until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned. I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, ablution. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came toward me and poured upon his hand and washed it, then he put his hand in and cupped it, and poured upon his hand once, then wiped over his head, then he scooped water with his hand and struck with it upon the back of his foot, and wiped with his hand over his foot. Then he came and prayed Zuhr for us."
